⁡u,\\,u=3x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is \n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=0.\n$$" 13194139533764 true] [17592186249856 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249857 13194139533764 true] [17592186249856 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249858 13194139533764 true] [17592186249856 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533764 true] [17592186249856 1041 "field-1" 13194139533764 true] [17592186249856 1104 #edb/ref 17592186249858 13194139533764 true] [17592186249856 1110 #uuid "16a10934-9000-5467-9780-1c375d10c554" 13194139533764 true] [17592186249857 1034 "3" 13194139533764 true] [17592186249857 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533764 true] [17592186249857 1111 #uuid "b5937a9f-fc76-5f26-945c-920b1984b07e" 13194139533764 true] [17592186249858 1034 "0" 13194139533764 true] [17592186249858 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533764 true] [17592186249858 1111 #uuid "6d5e87b6-f630-5904-b169-dff4595b1ae7" 13194139533764 true] [17592186249859 1017 #edb/ref 17592186249860 13194139533764 true] [17592186249859 1089 "q-310222" 13194139533764 true] [17592186249859 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533764 true] [17592186249859 1100 "Given that $f(x)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2{x}^{3}),$ we have\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n\n{{field-1}}." 13194139533764 true] [17592186249859 1113 #uuid "0c90cfa9-0486-5203-9da6-c4a1b9ecc483" 13194139533764 true] 